cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "QOREgeo: spatial intelligence for Python with zero dependencies"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Suneel Bose
    family-names: Karmegam
    email: suneelbosekarmegam@gmail.com
    affiliation: ArcGX TechLabs Private Limited
repository-code: "https://github.com/bosekarmegam/qoregeo"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/qoregeo"
abstract: >-
  QOREgeo is a pure-Python geospatial library that performs distance and
  bearing calculation, geodesic buffering, geofencing, shapefile and GPX/KML
  reading, density-based and k-means clustering, spatial joins, point-pattern
  statistics, route optimisation and interactive and static map rendering
  without any external dependency or compiled extension. It is designed for
  environments where the conventional geospatial stack cannot be installed,
  including serverless runtimes, embedded devices and restricted desktops.
keywords:
  - geospatial
  - GIS
  - Python
  - spatial analysis
  - geofencing
  - shapefile
  - clustering
  - spatial join
  - route optimisation
  - cartography
license: MIT
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-26"
